"""Direct question-design review of Christian and Islamic histories."""
from review_angle_plans import revise_domain, audit

CHRISTIAN = """history_origins|A Christian Community in the Record|Which dated sources establish one community's early presence in a place?|Compare inscriptions, manuscripts, archaeology, and later origin traditions.
famous_examples|A Council or Church in Context|What did one well-known council or institution actually decide or do?|Read surviving acts, participants, later reception, and omitted voices.
hidden_stories|Everyday Work of a Christian Community|Whose teaching, care, craft, or household labor is missing from standard histories?|Use local archives, material evidence, and consented accounts.
beginner_explainers|Many Christian Histories|How did two named churches develop differently in comparable periods?|Define doctrine, governance, language, and local context separately.
advanced_concepts|Authority and Church Governance|How did a named community determine authority over one issue?|Compare canons, councils, local practice, and later interpretation.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Uncertain Early Text|What evidence supports a disputed date or author for one Christian source?|Check manuscript witnesses, citations, language, and gaps.
technology_innovation|Digitizing a Church Archive|Can digital access clarify a community's history without exposing private records?|Check provenance, consent, metadata, and missing collections.
people_personalities|A Leader in Contemporary Sources|What can one figure's letters or acts establish about their role?|Separate surviving testimony from later hagiography.
major_events|A Community Before and After Reform|What changed after one dated council, law, or migration?|Compare institutions, liturgy, property, and members' lives.
how_it_works|A Historical Church Institution|How did one church body make decisions and deliver support?|Use statutes, minutes, accounts, and local testimony.
rise_fall|A Congregation's Changing Size|Why did one community grow or contract?|Check migration, conversion, births, law, census definitions, and record survival.
then_vs_now|One Christian Community Across Generations|Which practices and institutions changed?|Compare dated records with consented living accounts.
future_developments|Preserving a Living Church Site|Which conservation option supports both worship and heritage?|Compare material assessment, custodians, access, and funding.
myths_vs_facts|A Single Christian Position?|Does one common historical claim fit multiple named churches?|Compare their documents, not an assumed universal doctrine.
documentary_stories|One Community Through Its Archives|What do letters, registers, and photographs reveal about change?|Explain archive provenance, silences, and privacy limits.
text_source|A Church Document in Context|What does one canon, sermon, letter, or register actually say?|Cite author, date, language, intended audience, edition, and translation.
interpretive_lineages|Different Readings of One Event|How do two Christian communities interpret a shared historical event?|Attribute memory and compare dated records.
lived_practice|A Tradition as Lived Here|How does one present community explain its continuity and change?|Use consented voices and avoid universalizing.
ritual_sequence|An Observance in the Historical Record|What can sources establish about a named community's public worship?|Distinguish normative liturgy from observed local practice.
language_translation|A Theological Term Across Languages|How did translation affect one historical disagreement?|Compare original terms, context, and later usage.
regional_variants|Two Churches in Different Regions|How did similar institutions develop under different local conditions?|Match period and source type; explain law, language, and patronage.
art_and_devotion|An Object in Christian Use|What can one image or building reveal about community devotion?|Use provenance, patronage, liturgical setting, and living interpretation.
community_memory|Remembering a Changed Parish|How do oral accounts relate to registers and local archives?|Protect consent and present memory and documents distinctly.
ethics_in_context|A Church's Harmful Policy|How did one institution enact, defend, and later address a documented harmful rule?|Use official records and affected people's testimony, without collective blame.
source_and_history|A Manuscript's Evidential Limits|What can one Christian manuscript establish about a text's history?|Distinguish composition, copying, translation, and later use.
encounter_and_exchange|Christians and Their Neighbors|What records show interaction with another community in one place?|Compare multiple perspectives on trade, learning, cooperation, and conflict.
contemporary_voice|A Community Chooses Its Story|What history do current members consider important to preserve?|Use consent and include internal differences.
field_source_tradition|A Text Across Church Traditions|Which versions of one source survive and how do they differ?|Compare edition, manuscript line, language, and canon context.
field_lived_practice|A Local Church Today|How do present observances connect to dated community records?|Ask members and avoid assigning continuity from outside.
field_regional_variation|One Practice Across Regions|Which variation is supported by comparable evidence?|Match church tradition, time, and local context.
field_translation_issue|A Contested Historical Word|How did rendering a source term affect later interpretation?|Compare original usage, grammar, and translations.
field_intercommunity_contact|A Documented Encounter|What do both communities' records reveal about one exchange?|Identify archival imbalance and competing memories."""

ISLAMIC = """history_origins|A Muslim Community in Its Earliest Sources|Which dated records show a named community forming in one place?|Compare inscriptions, documents, archaeology, and later chronicles.
famous_examples|A Well-Known Islamic Institution|What did one mosque, school, court, or charitable foundation actually do?|Read endowment deeds, accounts, legal records, and local context.
hidden_stories|Workers and Households in Islamic History|Whose contributions are lost in a rulers-and-battles account?|Use letters, waqf records, objects, and attributed community voices.
beginner_explainers|Many Histories of Muslim Communities|How did two communities differ in law, language, and institutions?|Name place and period; avoid a single civilizational arc.
advanced_concepts|Law and Local Administration|How did one community apply a legal principle in a specific institution?|Compare juristic text, court record, governance, and practice.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Chronicle's Contested Date|What evidence supports or weakens one historical attribution?|Check manuscripts, citations, coinage, and archaeological context.
technology_innovation|Digitizing an Islamic Manuscript|What can a digital collection reveal and what provenance remains uncertain?|Check catalogue, ownership marks, transcription, and access.
people_personalities|A Scholar in the Source Record|What do writings and contemporary records establish about one figure?|Separate documented work from later biographical tradition.
major_events|A Community Across a Political Change|What changed after one dated conquest, reform, or migration?|Compare institutions, taxes, language, and household evidence.
how_it_works|A Historical Waqf or School|How did one foundation fund and govern a public service?|Read founding deed, later accounts, disputes, and beneficiaries.
rise_fall|An Institution's Changing Resources|Why did one mosque, school, or court expand or contract?|Use endowment, staffing, state policy, and local records.
then_vs_now|A Muslim Neighborhood Across Generations|Which institutions and practices changed?|Compare dated maps, archives, and consented living accounts.
future_developments|Preserving a Living Heritage Site|Which proposal protects material fabric and continuing community use?|Consider custodians, access, conservation, and funding.
myths_vs_facts|A Single Islamic Historical Story?|Does a common generalization fit diverse communities and periods?|Compare named sources without treating one region as universal.
documentary_stories|One Community in Manuscripts and Archives|What do records reveal about everyday life and political change?|State provenance, language, archive gaps, and later interpretation.
text_source|A Historical Islamic Text in Context|What does one document, chronicle, or legal passage actually record?|Cite author, date, manuscript, audience, translation, and genre.
interpretive_lineages|Different Memories of One Event|How do named Muslim communities interpret a shared historical event?|Attribute each tradition and compare dated evidence.
lived_practice|A Tradition in One Community|How do present members explain continuity and change?|Use consented accounts without universalizing.
ritual_sequence|An Observance in Historical Sources|What do records show about one community's public observance?|Distinguish prescriptive texts from documented local practice.
language_translation|An Arabic or Other Term in Context|How does translation alter one historical claim?|Compare original language, period usage, and later rendering.
regional_variants|Two Muslim Communities Compared|Why did comparable institutions differ across regions?|Align period, legal environment, language, and evidence.
art_and_devotion|An Islamic Object in Use|What can one manuscript, inscription, or building reveal?|Use provenance, patronage, function, and community interpretation.
community_memory|Remembering a Mosque or School|How do local accounts and archives depict one place?|Present attributed memory beside dated material records.
ethics_in_context|A Documented Unequal Rule|How did a named institution apply and later debate one unequal policy?|Read legal and administrative records with affected voices; avoid sweeping claims.
source_and_history|The Journey of a Manuscript|What can ownership notes and copies establish about a text's circulation?|Distinguish composition, copying, translation, and collection history.
encounter_and_exchange|Muslim and Neighboring Communities|What records show learning, trade, cooperation, or conflict in one setting?|Use sources from multiple parties and note asymmetries.
contemporary_voice|A Community's Own Heritage Priorities|What do current members want preserved in their history?|Use consent and represent internal variation.
field_source_tradition|A Chronicle Across Witnesses|Which versions support one historical account?|Compare manuscript dates, citations, translations, and later editing.
field_lived_practice|A Local Muslim Community Today|How do present practices relate to documented local history?|Ask members and avoid inferring uniform continuity.
field_regional_variation|One Institution in Two Regions|Which differences can comparable records establish?|Match time, legal setting, and source type.
field_translation_issue|A Word in an Islamic Archive|What changes when one historical term is translated?|Compare original context, genre, and period usage.
field_intercommunity_contact|A Traceable Encounter|What do records from both sides show about one exchange?|Identify missing archives and avoid a one-sided narrative."""

if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("284", "284_christianity_history", CHRISTIAN,
                  "Histories of named Christian communities across regions and denominations, their institutions, texts, everyday life, and living memory.",
                  "dated church and civic archives, manuscripts, council and legal records, inscriptions, material objects, and consented community accounts",
                  "Name church, place, and period; distinguish normative theology from documented practice and later memory. Avoid a single Christian trajectory or collective blame; protect private and affected voices.")
    revise_domain("285", "285_islamic_history", ISLAMIC,
                  "Histories of named Muslim communities across regions, their institutions, manuscripts, law in practice, everyday life, and living memory.",
                  "dated manuscripts, waqf deeds, court and civic records, inscriptions, material objects, archival provenance, and consented community accounts",
                  "Name community, place, and period; distinguish religious texts, juristic interpretation, administrative practice, and later memory. Avoid reducing Islamic history to one region, dynasty, or conflict.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
